        "aliases": [],
        "name": "Emerging Memory Devices for Neuromorphic Computing (EMDNC)",
        "credits": "4",
        "offered_to": [
            "UG (third and fourth year)",
            "PG"
        ],
        "department": null,
        "description": "This course provides an in-depth understanding of emerging non-volatile memories\u2014Resistive Random Access Memories (ReRAM), Phase Change RAM (PCRAM), Ferroelectric RAM (FeRAM), and Magnetic RAM (MRAM)\u2014with emphasis on their physical principles, switching mechanisms, and material engineering. It covers charge, spin, and ion transport processes governing device performance and scalability, and explores how these memories enable artificial synapses and neurons for neuromorphic computing.",
